[O-])[O-]","Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-000281","value":"16.4","numeric":16.4}}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"Ru1","value":-2.06,"value_relation":"=","std":0.23,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"0.9% NaCl","doi":"10.1002/anie.202006089","year":2020,"counterion":"[O-][Cl+3]([O-])([O-])[O-].[O-][Cl+3]([O-])([O-])[O-]","record_id":"MLDB-000015","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The lipophilicities of the Ru(II) complexes were determined according to the previously reported method.[5] Octanol-saturated water (OSW) and water-saturated octanol (WSO) were prepared by mixing octanol and saline. Aliquots of stock solutions of the ruthenium complexes in OSW were added to equalvolumes of WSO and shaken at 60 rpm. After 24 h, the sample was centrifuged at 3000 rpm for 10 min. Theaqueous and octanol layers were carefully separated into test tubes and analysed by UV-Vis spectroscopy.Partition coefficients of ruthenium complexes were calculated using the equation:log Po/w = log ([Ru]OSW / [Ru]WSO) (1)"}],"ccdc":["NUVLIC"]}